1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,270
♪I stretch and yawn
when the sun is high in the sky♪

2
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,030
♪A cup of tea and a little tune,
what a carefree life♪

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:28,480
♪The fortune teller said
love would come my way this year♪

4
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,580
♪But all I see is my food
arriving right on time♪

5
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,670
♪No rush, no worries♪

6
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,360
♪Love is all a matter of chance♪

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,480
♪Flowers bloom and fade♪

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,380
♪I'd rather take good care
of myself first♪

9
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,580
♪Two orioles sing among
the green willows♪

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,970
♪And I still don't have a boyfriend♪

11
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,590
♪My best years are nothing
to worry about♪

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,240
♪I'll stay happily single
till I'm old and gray♪

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,540
=Besties' Coming Fortune=

14
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,980
=Episode 22=

15
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:17,120
Sister.

16
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:19,920
Sister, what are you looking for?

17
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,000
Sister.

18
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:35,200
I remember everything now.

19
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,310
Yue.

20
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:42,670
Shuang.

21
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:45,080
Qin.

22
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,120
And Chuchu.

23
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:54,030
We were all dancing girls
at Wangyue Pavilion.

24
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:56,560
That year, we'd finally saved

25
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:57,560
enough money to buy our freedom.

26
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,870
We were ready to return
to our hometowns.

27
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:01,920
But that night,

28
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,150
a group of soldiers suddenly arrived

29
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:05,670
and dragged us into the military camp.

30
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:07,760
They forced us to drink poison

31
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,440
that would spread disease,

32
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:11,880
then sent us to serve in the enemy camp
as military prostitutes.

33
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:13,830
Once the disease spread,

34
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:16,040
they could defeat the enemy

35
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:18,600
without shedding a drop of blood.

36
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:20,760
It was the Marquis

37
00:02:21,590 --> 00:02:23,040
and his wife who stepped forward

38
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:24,640
to stop the Third Prince.

39
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,210
With a major battle approaching

40
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,590
and the enemy outnumbering us
ten to one,

41
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:33,360
if we don't resort
to extraordinary measures,

42
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,710
we'll all die here.

43
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:39,040
They're just a few lowly women.

44
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,270
Poisoning them
and sending them into the enemy camp

45
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:42,030
(Marquise Jingyuan)

46
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:43,710
will let us defeat
the enemy without a fight.

47
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:45,920
What?

48
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:47,510
Madam,

49
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,320
do you have a better plan?

50
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:53,270
When a woman can save the nation alone,

51
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,550
what need is there for a general?

52
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:58,760
These women are innocent.

53
00:02:58,870 --> 00:02:59,920
They're not pawns.

54
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:00,880
They're human beings.

55
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,990
Using them to spread disease
in the enemy camp

56
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:06,040
is no different
from taking innocent lives.

57
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:09,830
Come now,

58
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:12,320
Madam.

59
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,480
These women

60
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,310
make their living

61
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:17,920
entertaining men.

62
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,480
They're lowborn to begin with.

63
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,590
Giving them the chance

64
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:22,600
to serve the imperial court

65
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:24,200
is already a great honor.

66
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:25,760
Your Highness, do you know

67
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:28,600
why they ended up in such circumstances?

68
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:33,480
She...

69
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:34,960
Her father died in battle,

70
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:35,830
and her mother remarried.

71
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:38,320
Her relatives sold her to a brothel.

72
00:03:39,430 --> 00:03:40,760
A disaster struck her hometown.

73
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,270
Her entire family starved to death.

74
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:43,480
She sold herself

75
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:46,950
just to afford a simple coffin
for her mother.

76
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:49,320
Her husband joined the army

77
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:50,880
and was never heard from again.

78
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:52,360
She

79
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,590
was driven out by her husband's family

80
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:54,360
and had nowhere to turn.

81
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:56,390
These women weren't born inferior.

82
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,920
They had no control over their fate.

83
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,750
Only if we win this battle

84
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:01,480
and bring peace to the land

85
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:04,270
can they live with dignity.

86
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:06,480
We're fighting this war

87
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:08,400
so that women like them

88
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,760
can live decent lives,

89
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:11,390
not to sacrifice their lives

90
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:13,230
for a fleeting peace.

91
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,320
Madam,

92
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:25,080
you certainly have some nerve.

93
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:27,450
Are you trying to tell me what to do?

94
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:28,590
Dear.

95
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:34,800
He...

96
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:37,350
Your Highness.

97
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:38,800
Such disgraceful tactics

98
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,020
(Marquis Jingyuan)
are beneath contempt.

99
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:41,830
If you insist on proceeding,

100
00:04:42,430 --> 00:04:43,240
then my Shen family army

101
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:44,900
will have no choice but
to fight the enemy on our own.

102
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,000
I urge Your Highness

103
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,830
to reconsider.

104
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:52,560
The Marquis is right.

105
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,680
I failed to think this through.

106
00:04:56,510 --> 00:04:57,240
Release the women.

107
00:04:58,630 --> 00:04:59,440
Thank you, Your Highness.

108
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,030
Please, get up.

109
00:05:01,950 --> 00:05:02,710
Come, get up.

110
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:03,560
Please, rise.

111
00:05:05,190 --> 00:05:05,680
Get up.

112
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,080
Hurry.

113
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:08,350
Come on.

114
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:20,350
Disobeying military orders

115
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:21,990
and releasing prisoners
without authorization

116
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,080
is tantamount to treason.

117
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:25,950
Madam,

118
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:27,590
you didn't really think

119
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,640
I'd let you leave here alive, did you?

120
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,680
Marquis Jingyuan led his troops
into battle without authorization

121
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:44,880
and defied his commander's orders,

122
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,000
causing

123
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:48,240
tens of thousands of elite soldiers
to die in battle.

124
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,640
For these crimes, he deserves death.

125
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,300
The Marquis and his wife

126
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:10,240
died trying to save us.

127
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:20,510
Third Prince,

128
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,440
you monster!

129
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,320
I'll make sure he pays with his life.

130
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,240
The other sisters knew
they wouldn't survive.

131
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,590
But they said

132
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:39,680
we couldn't let the Marquis

133
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,560
and his wife die for nothing.

134
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:42,590
Drink it.

135
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,680
If you go to the enemy camp,

136
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,680
you'll be dying for your country.

137
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:49,350
I'll remember your contributions.

138
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:54,320
What you've done today

139
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,680
will one day

140
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:57,950
earn you the contempt
of the whole world.

141
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,080
Unfortunately,

142
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:00,800
that day

143
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,080
will never come.

144
00:07:23,390 --> 00:07:23,830
No!

145
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:27,950
If you don't drink the poison,

146
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,000
I'll kill you all right now.

147
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:48,680
Qin.

148
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,950
Qin!

149
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:52,590
Stay alive.

150
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,200
Yue

151
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,680
told me to hide it well,

152
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,270
somewhere no one would ever find it.

153
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:10,080
I've kept it hidden all these years.

154
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,240
Now,

155
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,880
it's time to give it to you.

156
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,977
(We fifteen dancing girls,
victims of the Third Prince,)

157
00:08:48,977 --> 00:08:50,780
(write this testimony in tears and blood.)

158
00:08:57,980 --> 00:08:58,776
(May future generations who read this)

159
00:08:58,776 --> 00:08:59,840
(restore the Marquis
and his wife's innocence)

160
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,320
Shen Cheng.

161
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,200
I, Shen Cheng,

162
00:09:23,510 --> 00:09:24,590
swear to seek justice for my parents

163
00:09:26,150 --> 00:09:28,280
and these innocent women

164
00:09:28,790 --> 00:09:30,040
who died so tragically.

165
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:33,750
Count me in.

166
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:37,830
Me too.

167
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,620
- We'll do it together.
- We'll do it together.

168
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,320
♪No matter how
the universe changes tomorrow♪

169
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:52,520
♪Right now, I just want
to stay by your side♪

170
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:57,720
♪Let this kiss and this dream
last until we're old♪

171
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:03,960
♪And hold on to all
the tenderness of this moment♪

172
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:10,400
♪Following this heartbeat,
we'll retrace our steps♪

173
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:16,880
♪As time goes by,
all I need is your gaze♪

174
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:21,520
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪

175
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:43,640
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪
